course: dictionary
lesson: 1503
title: Ceiling: the top of the room, and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A ceiling is the inside surface at the top of a room, above your head. Read the words around it to be sure. «Hot air rises and gathers at the ceiling first» tells you where warm air goes: up, to the top of the room.
explain: Ceiling can also mean an upper limit that something cannot go above, like a price ceiling. Ask: what word would fit here? In «a price ceiling», a top limit fits better than a room, so the meaning is the highest the price can go.
explain: Some phrases use ceiling in special ways. «Hit the ceiling» does not mean a bang on the roof; it means getting very angry. «Glass ceiling» means an unfair limit that stops people getting ahead. Swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
explain: Your sentence «Many spiders walk up glass and across ceilings» shows that some creatures can walk upside down on a ceiling. Context helps you see the picture, but a dictionary is the final check when you are unsure.
fact: A ceiling is the inside surface at the top of a room.
fact: Smoke alarms are fixed on the ceiling because smoke rises.
fact: In a fire, crawl low under smoke, because the air near the ceiling is hot and full of smoke.
fact: A ceiling can mean an upper limit, like a price ceiling.
fact: «Hit the ceiling» means to get very angry, and «glass ceiling» means an unfair limit on getting ahead.
exercise: «Hot air and smoke rise and fill a room from the ceiling down.» Where does the smoke gather first? | The windows | The door | The floor | *The ceiling
exercise: Jo says, «There is a price ceiling on bread this year.» What does ceiling mean here? | The floor of the shop | *The highest limit the price cannot go above | A kind of cloud | A cheap price
exercise: What does «hit the ceiling» mean? | *Get very angry | Clean the lights | Jump up to touch the roof | Paint the walls white
test: «Water from an overflowing bath can leak through the floor into the ceiling below.» What is the ceiling in this sentence? | The floor of the bath | A kind of cloud | The roof of the house | *The inside top of the room below
test: Why are smoke alarms fixed on the ceiling? | Ceilings are cheaper | Smoke sinks to the floor | Alarms like the dark | *Because smoke rises
exam: What does «floor to ceiling» mean? | A ceiling fan that turns | A tiny gap under the door | *From the bottom to the top of a room | A limit on how much you can spend
